[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487261507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98295#issuecomment-2487261507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98295","id":2487261507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UQJlD","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T03:17:39Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T05:54:44Z","body":"There is no bug. You just mixed up value track and bezier track those have different paths. Although it is not recommended, adding the initial value of the missing bezier track to the reset animation solves this problem.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b25b3414-6a16-4373-9ee0-27458bd8cff2)\n\nJust be aware that the value and bezier tracks with different paths (\"position\" vs \"position:x\") cannot be blended/xfaded. As long as you do not use xfade, the solution described above should work.\n\n[Maou.Test.Project_fixed.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17824178/Maou.Test.Project_fixed.zip)\n","author_associa